The Culinary &amp; Menu Operations Assistant supports the Culinary and Menu teams by owning in-week menu asks, operational coordination, and cross-functional communication. This role is designed to reduce ad-hoc operational workload on Recipe Developers, enabling them to focus on recipe output, quality, and strategic initiatives while supporting Menu Planning and Product teams during a period of increased scale.

This is a mid-level, execution-focused contract role ideal for an early-career candidate interested in food, operations, and large-scale menu development.

Lettuce share what this role will be responsible for:

•
Menu &amp; In-Week Operations&nbsp;

• Upkeep and ordering of Test kitchen supplies, including meal kits, groceries and tools.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Triage and manage in-week menu requests for HelloFresh and Chef’s Plate

• Act as the first point of contact for operational menu questions

• Track, document, and close menu-related asks using established tools and trackers

• Ensure requests meet defined guardrails before escalation

Cross-Functional Coordination&nbsp;

• Liaise with Menu Planning, Product, Editorial, and Procurement on day-to-day menu questions&nbsp;

• Support Menu Planning teams with overflow operational tasks where culinary development is not required&nbsp;

• Maintain clear communication and timely follow-ups across teams&nbsp;

Culinary Team Enablement&nbsp;

• Create systems to update recipes with limited Recipe Developer input&nbsp;

• Support basic data entry, documentation, and tracker hygiene&nbsp;

• Assist with preparation for tastings, menu reviews, and internal meetings as needed&nbsp;

Process Support &amp; Improvement&nbsp;

• Identify recurring in-week issues and flag opportunities for process improvement&nbsp;

• Support standardization of intake forms, templates, and SOPs

• All other duties, as assigned

Sound a-peeling? Here's what we're looking for:&nbsp;

• 2+ years of experience in food, operations, coordination, or administrative roles&nbsp;

• Strong organizational and communication skills&nbsp;

• Comfortable working across multiple teams and priorities&nbsp;

• Detail-oriented, proactive, and calm under pressure&nbsp;

• Interest in food or culinary operations is an asset, but not required

